**Mapbox** is the definitive free-tier solution for port-city landmark and distance extraction, offering **100,000 geocoding requests per month** with explicit commercial use rights, production-grade data quality, and zero cost for a 1-person agency as of June 2026[1].

| Feature | Detail |
| :--- | :--- |
| **Free Tier Limits** | 100,000 requests/month; 600 req/min burst[1] |
| **API Endpoint Format** | `https://api.mapbox.com/geocoding/v5/mapbox.places/{QUERY}.json?access_token={TOKEN}&types=place,poi,landmark`[1] |
| **Concrete 30-Second Step** | In your Node/Python script, install the client (`npm install @mapbox/mapbox-sdk` or `pip install mapbox`), initialize it with your public token, and call `sdk.geocodingReverseGeocode({lat: 40.7, lon: -74.0})` to instantly resolve a port coordinate to a landmark name and distance string[1]. |

For **US-only** ports, the **US Census Geocoder** is unbeatable (completely free, unlimited, no restrictions), but Mapbox is superior for global coverage and landmark specificity[1]. Avoid "free" credits from Google (covers ~28,500 requests before hitting $5/1k) or demo-only APIs like Maps.co (25k cap, demo only) as they lack the headroom for commercial volume[1]. OpenCage is a viable alternative (2,500/day) but offers less throughput than Mapbox[1].

**Integration Code Snippet (Node.js):**
```javascript
const MapboxSDK = require('@mapbox/mapbox-sdk');
const sdk = new MapboxSDK({ accessToken: 'YOUR_PUBLIC_TOKEN' });

sdk.geocodingForwardGeocode({ query: 'Port of New York landmark' })
  .send()
  .then(response => {
    const landmark = response.body.features[0].place_name;
    const distance = response.body.features[0].distance; // meters from center
    console.log(`Found: ${landmark}, Distance: ${distance}m`);
  });
```
This approach ensures your agency extracts precise landmark names and distances from port coordinates without exceeding budget[1].
